      "hints": ["Track one distinctive tile in each row: which way does it move, and where does it re-enter?","Check that the two rows move in opposite directions, then follow the pointer.","Predict both rows, the pointer and the background before looking at the options."],
      "solution": ["Top row: the tiles slide one place to the right each step; the tile that leaves one end re-enters at the other. Next: vertical stripes, white, grey, rising diagonal hatching.","Bottom row: the tiles slide one place to the left, wrapping round. Next: rising diagonal hatching, grey, chequers, horizontal stripes.","Pointer: up-right → right → down-right → down → down-left, turning 45° clockwise each step. Next: left.","Background: grey → white → grey → white → grey. Next: white."],
      "explanation": "Four independent rules apply: the top row slides one tile to the right; the bottom row slides one tile to the left; the pointer turns 45° clockwise; the background alternates. Work out each rule from consecutive frames, predict the next frame, then eliminate. Option similarity alone is not evidence of a rule.",
